content:
{
  "asset": "Pump P-113, AquaDyne HF-300 end-suction centrifugal pump, serial HF3-22650",
  "priority": "P2",
  "stop_equipment_now": false,
  "condition_assessment": [
    {
      "statement": "The drive-end vibration is 4.8 mm/s. The applicable limit is Figure 3 of the HF-300 O&M manual, using the highest bearing-housing reading. 4.8 mm/s is above the 4.5 mm/s Zone B/C boundary and below the 7.1 mm/s Zone C/D boundary, so it is in Zone C: 'Restricted - plan maintenance'. It is not in Zone D ('Damage likely - stop the pump'), so an immediate stop is not required by the manual. This assumes the reading is velocity RMS taken on the bearing housing, as Figure 3 specifies.",
      "citations": [
        "C06",
        "C07"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "The bearing housing temperature is 70 C. The applicable limit is the manual specification of normal up to 70 C, alarm at 80 C and trip at 90 C, measured on the housing surface. 70 C is at the upper edge of normal, 10 C below alarm and 20 C below trip. No action is triggered, but there is no margin left and it must be trended.",
      "citations": [
        "C02",
        "C01"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "No leakage is reported, so the seal shows no troubleshooting symptom. Seal replacement is not part of this work order.",
      "citations": [
        "C09"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Both readings started after the motor was replaced. The manual requires laser alignment after any work that moves the motor. Misalignment is listed as a cause of both high vibration and high bearing temperature.",
      "citations": [
        "C10",
        "C09"
      ]
    }
  ],
  "probable_causes": [
    {
      "statement": "Shaft misalignment after the motor replacement (most likely). The motor was moved, which triggers the section 5.4 laser-alignment requirement. Misalignment is the first listed cause of high vibration and also explains the bearing temperature sitting at the 70 C limit of normal.",
      "citations": [
        "C10",
        "C09",
        "C02"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Bearing wear or damage, for example from running misaligned. This is a listed cause of high vibration and high bearing temperature.",
      "citations": [
        "C09"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Impeller imbalance or damage. This is a listed cause of high vibration, but it is less likely given that the onset coincided with the motor work.",
      "citations": [
        "C09"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Cavitation or insufficient NPSH. This is a listed cause of high vibration, but it is less likely unless suction conditions also changed.",
      "citations": [
        "C09"
      ]
    }
  ],
  "tasks": [
    {
      "statement": "Before stopping, measure vibration velocity (mm/s RMS) on both bearing housings, drive end and non-drive end. Classify the highest reading using Figure 3. If any reading reaches Zone D (above 7.1 mm/s), stop the pump immediately. Record the housing temperature; if it reaches the 80 C alarm, escalate.",
      "citations": [
        "C06",
        "C07",
        "C02"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Schedule a planned stop. Isolate the pump and motor before work (the site isolation procedure applies; see safety controls).",
      "citations": [
        "C07",
        "C10"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Perform laser shaft alignment of motor to pump as required after any work that moves the motor (manual 5.4). Alignment tolerances: parallel offset 0.05 mm, angular 0.05 mm per 100 mm. Record as-found and as-left values.",
      "citations": [
        "C10"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "If the bearing housing is disturbed, tighten the bearing housing bolts (M12) to 85 Nm, lightly oiled threads. The torque for the motor hold-down bolts is not documented; see open questions.",
      "citations": [
        "C11"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Restart, ensuring the pump is primed and the Plan 11 seal flush is available (never run dry). Re-measure vibration on both housings and the housing temperature. Target Zone A/B (4.5 mm/s or below) for long-term operation, with temperature 70 C or below.",
      "citations": [
        "C02",
        "C07"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "If vibration stays above 4.5 mm/s or temperature stays high after alignment, follow the troubleshooting table. Check grease quantity for over-greasing, inspect the bearings and impeller, and check NPSH.",
      "citations": [
        "C09"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "If either bearing shows wear, noise or high temperature, replace both bearings as a pair (manual 5.3). This needs the back pull-out assembly removed. Fit a new casing gasket whenever the casing is opened, and tighten casing bolts (M16) to 210 Nm and the impeller nut (M24) to 160 Nm.",
      "citations": [
        "C10",
        "C05",
        "C11"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Contingency only: if the seal is disturbed during any teardown on this serial (HF3-22650), do NOT fit HF3-450. Fit cartridge seal HF3-450B, which needs no sleeve measurement. Torque its gland nuts to 30 Nm, not the 25 Nm in Table 5. Replace shaft sleeve HF3-455 if scoring exceeds 0.1 mm depth.",
      "citations": [
        "C13",
        "C11"
      ]
    }
  ],
  "parts": [
    {
      "part_number": "HF3-512",
      "description": "Drive-end bearing 6312-C3. CONTINGENT: only if inspection shows wear; replace as a pair with HF3-510.",
      "quantity": 1,
      "citations": [
        "C05",
        "C10"
      ]
    },
    {
      "part_number": "HF3-510",
      "description": "Non-drive-end bearing 6310-C3. CONTINGENT: only if inspection shows wear; replace as a pair with HF3-512.",
      "quantity": 1,
      "citations": [
        "C05",
        "C10"
      ]
    },
    {
      "part_number": "HF3-120",
      "description": "Casing gasket. CONTINGENT: required if the casing is opened (back pull-out for bearing or impeller work).",
      "quantity": 1,
      "citations": [
        "C05",
        "C10"
      ]
    },
    {
      "part_number": "HF3-450B",
      "description": "Cartridge mechanical seal, replacing HF3-450 for serial HF3-22000 and above. CONTINGENT: only if the seal is disturbed or damaged during teardown.",
      "quantity": 1,
      "citations": [
        "C13"
      ]
    }
  ],
  "safety_controls": [
    {
      "statement": "Isolate the pump before any mechanical work, and drain it if the casing is to be opened.",
      "citations": [
        "C10"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Stop the pump immediately if vibration reaches Zone D (above 7.1 mm/s RMS). Respect the bearing temperature alarm at 80 C and trip at 90 C.",
      "citations": [
        "C07",
        "C02"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Never run the pump dry. Confirm the Plan 11 seal flush from discharge is in place on restart.",
      "citations": [
        "C02"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "The back pull-out assembly weighs 68 kg. Lifting equipment is required if it is removed.",
      "citations": [
        "C02"
      ]
    }
  ],
  "labour": [
    {
      "statement": "Laser alignment: 1.5 h, 1 technician (standard time).",
      "citations": [
        "C12"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Contingent bearing replacement (pair): 6.0 h, 2 technicians.",
      "citations": [
        "C12"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Contingent mechanical seal replacement: 4.0 h, 2 technicians, only if the seal is disturbed.",
      "citations": [
        "C12"
      ]
    }
  ],
  "source_conflicts": [
    {
      "statement": "The seal part and gland nut torque conflict between the documents. The O&M manual (Rev D) lists HF3-450 and a seal gland nut torque of 25 Nm. Service Bulletin SB-2026-014 (issued 14 March 2026) supersedes HF3-450 with HF3-450B at 30 Nm for HF-300 pumps with serial HF3-22000 and above. Serial HF3-22650 is in that range, so the bulletin applies. Use HF3-450B and 30 Nm; the manual seal part and 25 Nm gland torque must not be used on this pump. All other Table 5 torques are unaffected.",
      "citations": [
        "C05",
        "C11",
        "C13"
      ]
    }
  ],
  "open_questions": [
    "Was the motor aligned by the electrical contractor after replacement? Are as-left alignment records available?",
    "Which machine's drive end was measured (pump or motor bearing housing)? What is the non-drive-end reading? The manual requires classifying the highest reading of both housings.",
    "Was the 4.8 mm/s value velocity RMS on the bearing housing, as Figure 3 requires?",
    "What were the pre-replacement baseline vibration and housing temperature for P-113, to confirm the change is due to the motor work?",
    "The torque for the motor hold-down bolts and the coupling bolts is not given in the evidence.",
    "Does the replacement motor match the specified 1480 rpm, 55 kW, 400 V? Has rotation direction been verified?",
    "Have suction conditions/NPSH changed? No suction pressure data is provided.",
    "Were soft foot checks or shimming needed? Is there coupling type or condition information? Not covered by the evidence.",
    "The site lockout/isolation procedure details are not in the evidence."
  ]
}
